*  GIT.FURNIDS(REPO, IDS) — the account's furniture file ids, @AM-separated.
*  Copyright (C) 2026 Gordon Heydon.  GPL-2.0-only (see LICENSE).
*
*  ONE PLACE THAT ASKS THE QUESTION, for the same reason GIT.FILECLASS exists:
*  `add` and `status` have to agree exactly, or the account never reads clean.
*  When add dropped VOC's pointers to furniture (mv_git#78) and status did not
*  know to, every one of them came back as `?? VOC/_HOLD_` — untracked forever,
*  because the thing reporting them was the thing that would never stage them.
*
*  The rules themselves are NOT here.  They live in mv_account_furniture() in
*  the engine, one table per MV system, and this reaches them through the
*  FURNITURE op — which matches strings and reads no records, so mvgitd can
*  answer it on UniVerse just as in-session CallC does on UniData (mv_git#81).
*
*  Every file-type VOC id is a candidate, local or not: VOC points at furniture
*  that has no file in the account (_ENCINFO_, _KEYSTORE_), and those pointers
*  are furniture too.  What comes back is what the filter REMOVED, by
*  subtraction, so a caller cannot end up with a different answer than the one
*  the files themselves were chosen by.
      SUBROUTINE GIT.FURNIDS(REPO, IDS)
      $INCLUDE BP.INC PLATFORM.H
      AM = CHAR(254) ; VM = CHAR(253)
      IDS = ""
      ALLF = ""
      OPEN "VOC" TO FVOC ELSE
         RETURN
      END
*     THE PORTABLE SELECT FORM, for the reason GIT.STATUS records at its own
*     select: a bare `SELECT x` with `LOOP WHILE READNEXT ... DO` does not parse
*     everywhere.  Select to a named list and read from it by name.
*     Assigned first: the list variable is an OUTPUT of SELECT, but it is read
*     before it is written, and an unassigned one is a fault message in the
*     middle of the verb's output.  Same spelling as GIT.STATUS and
*     GITUDT.CHECKOUT, which is the one all three platforms accept.
      FLIST = ""
      SELECT FVOC TO FLIST
      LOOP
         READNEXT FVID FROM FLIST ELSE EXIT
         READ FVREC FROM FVOC, FVID THEN
*           Attribute 1 is the type, but UniVerse appends any description given
*           at CREATE.FILE time — so take the first token, as the add walk does.
            FVT = TRIM(FIELD(FVREC<1>, " ", 1))
            IF FVT = "F" OR FVT = "DIR" THEN ALLF<-1> = FVID : VM : FVT
         END
      REPEAT
      CLEARSELECT
      IF ALLF = "" THEN RETURN
      FOUT = ""
      CALL GIT.OBJ("FURNITURE", 2, REPO, ALLF, "", "", "", FOUT)
*     The engine answers "" only on failure, and any account keeps at least VOC,
*     so an empty answer means the op did not run — report no furniture rather
*     than declare the whole account furniture.
      IF FOUT = "" THEN RETURN
      NALL = DCOUNT(ALLF, AM)
      FOR FK = 1 TO NALL
         LOCATE(ALLF<FK>, FOUT; FPOS) ELSE IDS<-1> = FIELD(ALLF<FK>, VM, 1)
      NEXT FK
      RETURN
      END
